            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0403" n="389" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg389"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/11–1044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-10T14:00:00+01:00">November 10,
                            1944—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 10—11:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9785. For the Under Secretary and Mr. Dunn. Reference Embassy’s 9776, November 9,
                    8 p.m. British Chiefs of Staff have today officially stated their opinion,
                    reported to Mosely by Strang, that the interim amendment regarding Bremen is
                    acceptable for inclusion in the Protocol on Zones provided the words “he
                    determines” can be changed to “may be agreed”. As this question was presented
                    fully in 9776 the Department’s comments and instructions will be awaited.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gallman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
